On 16 Mai, 19:22, Moonsilence <usene...@JUNKmoonsilence.de> wrote:

> On that matter, are creatures hatching from eggs in my inventory not
> always tame? Is there a spoiler on this? Until I noticed the nagas
> appearing, I always thought eggs were just another gimmick food item.

Eva Myers' pet spoiler (http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/slashem/
pets.html) has a bit of information on that subject, which I will now
shamelessly quote for you:

"Polymorphing yourself into a female egg-laying monster and laying an
egg is a useful technique for acquiring pets. Any egg laid by you is
guaranteed to hatch into a pet. You can also sometimes get pets from
eggs which you didn't lay, although this is probably less useful. Any
dragon egg which hatches while you are carrying it will become a tame
baby dragon. If you are male, any other egg which hatches while
carried by you has a 50% chance of yielding a pet."

Furthermore, Dylan's food spoiler (http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/
341/food-341.html) lists the probability of a pre-generated (i.e. not
laid by you) egg hatching as "roughly 1/3".

As a personal note, I'd like to add that I've very rarely seen generic
eggs hatching, despite the fact that I tend to carry lots of them in
my backpack (I never eat unidentified eggs unless I'm starving...
could be a cockatrice egg among them *shudder*). So I don't know what
to think of this "roughly 1/3 probability". If that's straight from
the source, it's gotta be true, of course. If it's just a guess,
though, I'm not really willing to believe it.



